  "goodToKnow": "Die Gattin is a formal word for wife: der Minister und seine Gattin. Der Gatte is the husband, and die Ehegatten are spouses, a term still used in German law and tax forms: das Ehegattensplitting is the tax rule for married couples. In daily life, Germans just say meine Frau or mein Mann. Ihre Gattin sounds polite but a bit old-fashioned. The root gatten means to join, as in die Gattung (genus, kind)."
